## Recalls on the Rise

This year alone, the FDA has processed 781 recalls, a significant increase over last year. Of these, 217 have been classified as Class I, the most severe tier, indicating a reasonable probability that exposure to the product will cause serious adverse health consequences or death. Notably, Adams Extract & Spice LLC made headlines this week with multiple recalls involving undeclared sesame allergens across a range of spice blends. These issues signal systemic labeling or cross-contamination problems that demand urgent correction.

## Repeat Offenders

Alarmingly, 95 brands have been flagged as repeat offenders this year. Among them, Spring & Mulberry Inc. and Moonlight Packing Corporation stand out with F-ratings for their consistent failure to meet safety standards. Spring & Mulberry Inc. has had 11 recalls, all classified as Class I, demonstrating a concerning pattern of negligence.

## Recent Highlights

On July 15, Fresh & Ready Foods LLC recalled two chicken sandwich products due to the use of raw breaded chicken patties, posing a Salmonella contamination risk. The products were not sold at retail but were distributed to employee breakrooms, raising questions about food safety in non-retail environments. Meanwhile, Adams Extract & Spice LLC was involved in a recall for undeclared sesame allergens in multiple spice products, further emphasizing the need for stricter allergen control measures.

## What's in Your Pantry?

With 1139 recalls in FDA history, consumers must stay vigilant. The top offenders this year have ranged across diverse categories, including seasoning mixes, baked goods, and dietary supplements. Brands like Wellnov Supplements LLC and Diva Fam Inc. continue to face scrutiny for recurring issues.

## Final Word

The shelf never lies. With a significant uptick in recalls and repeat offenses, it's clear that robust enforcement of safety standards is essential. Consumers, stay informed and proactive. Check your pantries and think twice before trusting brands with a history of negligence.
